# 13.1.7 Asynchronous Processing

Heavy operations shall execute asynchronously.

Examples

```
PDF Parsing

OCR

Embedding Generation

Neo4j Construction

Vector Indexing

Compliance Analysis

PDF Report Generation
```

These jobs shall be processed using Celery workers.

---

# 13.1.8 Event Flow

The system shall communicate using events.

Examples

```
DocumentUploaded

↓

TextExtracted

↓

ClausesExtracted

↓

EmbeddingsGenerated

↓

KnowledgeUpdated

↓

AnalysisStarted

↓

AnalysisCompleted

↓

ReportGenerated
```

This enables loose coupling between components.

---

# 13.1.9 Pipeline State Machine

Each processing job shall maintain a state.

```
Pending

↓

Queued

↓

Running

↓

Completed
```

Failure path

```
Running

↓

Failed

↓

Retrying

↓

Completed

or

Failed Permanently
```

The frontend shall display these states in real time.

---

# 13.1.10 Retry Strategy

Retryable operations

- OCR failure
- Embedding API timeout
- Neo4j connection error
- Qdrant timeout
- LLM timeout

Retries shall use exponential backoff.

Non-retryable failures shall be marked for administrator review.

---

# 13.1.11 Error Isolation

Failure in one document shall never interrupt processing of unrelated documents.

Every uploaded document shall have an independent processing workflow.

---

# 13.1.12 Parallel Processing

The following stages may execute concurrently where dependencies allow:

- OCR
- Metadata extraction
- Named Entity Recognition
- Embedding generation
- Graph relationship extraction

Parallel execution shall reduce total processing time.

---

# 13.1.13 Monitoring

Every stage shall expose metrics.

Examples

```
Processing Time

Success Rate

Failure Rate

Queue Length

Average Retrieval Time

Average LLM Latency

Embedding Duration
```

These metrics shall be available through the administration dashboard.

---

# 13.1.14 Logging

Every pipeline stage shall generate structured logs.

Each log entry shall include:

```
Timestamp

Document ID

Organization ID

Pipeline Stage

Status

Duration

Worker ID

Error Details (if applicable)
```

Logs shall exclude sensitive document content.

---

# 13.1.15 Audit Trail

Every compliance report shall maintain complete traceability.

The audit record shall include:

- Source document
- Retrieved legal clauses
- Graph nodes used
- Embeddings version
- Knowledge base version
- LLM model version
- Prompt version
- Report version

This enables complete reproducibility of analysis results.

---

# 13.1.16 Scalability

The pipeline shall support:

Multiple workers

Horizontal scaling

Independent worker queues

Distributed processing

Container deployment

Cloud-native execution

---

